  <article class="page about">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>I’m Bhishma Raj, a software engineer from Madurai, India. I use this site to keep track of what I’m working on and to write down my musings.</p>

    <figure class="portrait">
      <img src="/images/profile_pic_2019.jpeg" alt="Bhishma Raj" />
    </figure>

    <h2>From the old blog</h2>
    <p>I studied theoretical computer science at <a href="https://www.cmi.ac.in/">Chennai Mathematical Institute</a> after completing an undergraduate degree in computer science and engineering at Shiv Nadar University.</p>
    <p>I’m broadly interested in theoretical computer science—especially algorithms—and in psychology and its interaction with computing. Biology has influenced many computational constructions, from finite automata to neural networks and cellular automata, so I find the cognitive sciences particularly interesting.</p>
    <p>Not so long ago I used to game a lot. Competitive programming later took its place. I’m also a huge fan of MOOCs and find them a good way to get introduced to new subjects. At CMI, my friends and I also got interested in indoor rock climbing.</p>

