    <h2>Regarding the old name</h2>
    <blockquote><p>The curse of knowledge is a cognitive bias that occurs when someone unknowingly assumes that others have the background to understand.</p></blockquote>
    <p>The phrase named the original blog. It is a common phenomenon, and recognising biases like it can help us communicate and make decisions more clearly.</p>

